IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 265 (piece dg8, lines 1327 to 1347):
-- conversion of other entities to a domestic corporation.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation. Here that is a person in an other entity
-- that is converting (a member, partner, manager or owner who will be a stockholder, director or incorporator of the corporation
-- it becomes) or in the corporation it has become. The seat layer dg8-seat.l4 asks these rules from that side.
--
-- What the section leaves to law outside this module is an input, named for the fact with its section, and listed in NOTES.md:
--   * execution, acknowledgment, filing and the effective time of an instrument: sections 103 and 103(d) (piece dg1);
--   * when a corporation's existence commences ordinarily: section 106 (piece dg1), which subsection (d) displaces;
--   * what a corporation may do under Subchapter II (powers, sections 121 to 127: piece dg2);
--   * the governing writing of the other entity and the law applicable to it (approval of the conversion, of a plan of conversion,
--     winding up under non-Delaware law): not among the inputs.
-- Section 114(a) reads "stockholder" as "member" for a nonstock corporation; section 265 is not among the sections section 114(b) and (c) take out of that
-- reading, so "stockholder" below includes a member of a nonstock corporation.

§ `s 265(a) What an other entity is`

-- "Other entity": a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or
-- any other unincorporated business including a partnership (of the four kinds), or a foreign corporation. A predicate over the core `Entity`
-- (keel instruction 12). A corporation formed in this State is not an "other entity"; a corporation formed in any other jurisdiction is
-- (the core's rule for "foreign corporation", section 371(a): organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State).
-- A natural person is not an entity of any kind named.
-- src:1328 | (a) As used in this section, the term “other entity” means a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), or a foreign corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(a) (src:1328)
GIVEN e IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 265(a) the term other entity` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `kind of entity`
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation` kk THEN `the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` e
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `s 265(b) Filing to convert to a corporation of this State`

-- src:1329 | (b) Any other entity may convert to a corporation of this State by complying with subsection (h) of this section and filing in the office of the Secretary of State:
-- src:1330 | (1) A certificate of conversion to corporation that has been executed in accordance with subsection (i) of this section and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title; and
-- src:1331 | (2) A certificate of incorporation that has been executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
-- src:1332 | Each of the certificates required by this subsection (b) shall be filed simultaneously in the office of the Secretary of State and, if such certificates are not to become effective upon their filing as permitted by § 103(d) of this title, then each such certificate shall provide for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(b) (src:1329-1332)
GIVEN e IS AN Entity
      `the conversion was approved in accordance with subsection (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of conversion to corporation was executed in accordance with subsection (i) and filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the two certificates were filed simultaneously in the office of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificates are to become effective upon their filing as permitted by § 103(d)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103(d) (piece dg1)
      `each certificate provides for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 265(b) the other entity has converted to a corporation of this State by filing as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `s 265(a) the term other entity` e
    AND `the conversion was approved in accordance with subsection (h)`
    AND `the certificate of conversion to corporation was executed in accordance with subsection (i) and filed in accordance with § 103`
    AND `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`
    AND `the two certificates were filed simultaneously in the office of the Secretary of State`
    -- "if such certificates are not to become effective upon their filing ..., then each such certificate shall provide for the same effective date or time"
    AND (   `the certificates are to become effective upon their filing as permitted by § 103(d)`
         OR `each certificate provides for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d)`)

§ `s 265(c) The certificate of conversion to corporation`

-- src:1333 | (c) The certificate of conversion to corporation shall state:
-- src:1334 | (1) The date on which and jurisdiction where the other entity was first created, incorporated, formed or otherwise came into being and, if it has changed, its jurisdiction immediately prior to its conversion to a domestic corporation;
-- src:1335 | (2) The name and type of entity of the other entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate of conversion to corporation; and
-- src:1336 | (3) The name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation filed in accordance with subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:1337 | (4) If a plan of conversion is adopted in accordance with subsection (k) of this section, that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of such certificate in accordance with all law applicable to the other entity, including any approval required under such applicable law for the authorization of the type of corporate action specified in the plan of conversion.
